patrone-notepad (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * First package: Notepad, a plain text editor with tabs across the title
    bar and a + button for a new one; File, Edit and View menus with
    Settings at the end of their row; and a status bar with the cursor's
    line and column, the number of characters (and how many are selected),
    the zoom, the line endings and the encoding, the last two of which can
    be changed from there.
  * New tab, New window, Open, Save, Save as, Save all, Print, Close tab,
    Close window and Exit; Undo, Redo, Cut, Copy, Paste, Delete, Find, Find
    next and previous, Replace, Go to line, Select all, the time and date,
    and Font; Zoom, the status bar and word wrap.
  * Find and replace in a box over the text, finding as you type, with
    Match case and Wrap around.
  * Reads UTF-8 (with or without a byte order mark), UTF-16 and CP1252
    text, with LF, CRLF or CR line endings, and saves it the same way.
  * Settings: the app's theme (light, dark or the desktop's), the font
    (PatroneOS Mono, 11 points, by default), word wrap, whether files from
    other apps open in a new tab or a new window, and whether to restore
    open tabs: on, Notepad keeps the open tabs and their unsaved changes as
    you work (in ~/.local/state/patrone-notepad), without changing the
    files, and brings them back when it starts; off, it starts with a new
    tab and asks to save changes when it closes.
  * The notepad command, its launcher entry and Patrone's own icon. Files
    can be dropped on the window to open them.

